# Helm chart templates are Go-templated YAML, which is NOT valid YAML — every one of these 21 files
# opens with `{{- if ... -}}`, and Prettier's YAML parser fails on it outright ("Block collections
# are not allowed within flow collections"). This is a hard parse error, not a formatting
# difference: Prettier can neither check nor rewrite them, so leaving them in scope would make
# `format:check` permanently red and un-fixable. Helm's own `helm lint` / `helm template` (CI job
# 4b, tools/helm-verify) is what actually validates these files.
deploy/helm/templates/
deploy/helm-bundled/templates/

# VENDORED UPSTREAM MANIFESTS — verbatim copies of Argo CD / Argo Workflows / Argo Events / Gitea
# install YAML, kept byte-identical to the release they were pulled from (charter principle 5: no
# runtime network calls, everything vendored). Reformatting them would rewrite ~183,000 lines of
# third-party artifact and, worse, destroy the property that makes them maintainable — a clean
# `diff` against the next upstream release. They are not ours to restyle.
deploy/helm-bundled/vendor/
